===Etymology===
{{suffix|Srbija|nac|lang=sh|sc=Latn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/srbijǎːnats/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|Sr|bi|ja|nac|lang=sh}}

===Proper noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=Srbijánac}}

# an inhabitant or a resident of region [[Serbia]]
# a citizen of country [[Serbia]]

====Usage notes====
{{unreferenced}}
The term {{m|sh|Sȑbin}} denotes an ethnic Serb, while the term {{m|sh|Srbijánac}} has a complex meaning since it is sometimes considered derogatory, but it should not be. It is a simple description of a person living in Serbia that has other ethnicities living there. It is a description that is mostly used by people from Bosnia, Croatia and other former republics of former Yugoslavia. It is not meant to be derogatory in any way since not only Serbs live in this country.

